# The app's own cache-busting (js/version.js -> sw.js's versioned
# CACHE_NAME, and the Settings caching toggle) only works if the browser —
# and Cloudflare, which fronts this host — actually re-fetch index.html and
# the app's JS/CSS instead of serving a stale copy out of the browser's own
# HTTP disk cache. That layer is completely separate from the Service
# Worker's Cache Storage: unregistering the SW and clearing its caches (what
# the Settings toggle does) has zero effect on it. Without this, a version
# bump can sit invisible on disk forever, because the browser never even
# fetches the new bytes to notice anything changed.
#
# no-cache (not no-store) still lets responses be cached, but forces a
# revalidation round-trip (conditional GET) before reuse, so an unchanged
# file is still a cheap 304 rather than a full re-download every load.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "^(index\.html|sw\.js|manifest\.json)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>

  <FilesMatch "\.(js|mjs|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
